# Citation registry

Canonical sources for this project. **URLs live here and nowhere else** — code and docs
cite the key (`[CIT-TTN-FUP]`) so a moved link is fixed in one place.

Governed by [`.cursor/rules/20-citation-discipline.mdc`](../.cursor/rules/20-citation-discipline.mdc).
Validated by [`scripts/check_citations.py`](../scripts/check_citations.py), which fails the
build on a reference to an undefined key and warns on any row still marked `UNVERIFIED`.

## Status values

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `VERIFIED` | Fetched on the date shown; the page resolved and contained the cited fact |
| `UNVERIFIED` | Believed correct but **not yet fetched** — verify before relying on it |
| `ACCESS-LIMITED` | Real and reachable in a browser, but blocked to automated fetching |
| `REGISTRATION` | Behind a login/registration wall |

Verifying an `UNVERIFIED` row means opening the URL, confirming it states the fact in the
"Establishes" column, and updating the status and date. Do not upgrade a row on memory.

## Network policy and LoRaWAN specification

| Key | Title | Publisher | URL | Establishes | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `CIT-TTN-FUP` | Duty Cycle — Fair Use Policy | The Things Network | https://www.thethingsnetwork.org/docs/lorawan/duty-cycle/ | Sandbox limits are **30 s uplink airtime per node per 24 h** and **10 downlink messages per node per 24 h**. Sets the airtime budget in rule 40. | VERIFIED 2026-07-30 |
| `CIT-TTN-FUP-EXPLAINED` | Fair Use Policy explained | TTN community forum | https://www.thethingsnetwork.org/forum/t/fair-use-policy-explained/1300 | Derives the 30 s figure as (8 channels × 86400 s × 5% gateway RX duty) ÷ 1000 nodes. States a 10-byte payload allows ~20 msg/day at SF12 vs ~500 at SF7, and that the downlink cap **includes ACKs for confirmed uplinks**. | VERIFIED 2026-07-30 |
| `CIT-TTN-FREQ` | Frequency Plans | The Things Network | https://www.thethingsnetwork.org/docs/lorawan/frequency-plans/ | US915 sub-band channel plan used by this node. | UNVERIFIED |
| `CIT-LORA-RP002` | RP002 Regional Parameters | LoRa Alliance | https://lora-alliance.org/resource_hub/rp2-regional-parameters/ | US915 channel plan, DR0–DR13, per-DR max payload (DR0 = 11 bytes application payload), RX2 default frequency and data rate. | REGISTRATION |
| `CIT-LW-LINK` | LoRaWAN Link Layer Specification | LoRa Alliance | https://lora-alliance.org/resource_hub/lorawan-specification-v1-0-4/ | Class A opens exactly two receive windows (RX1, RX2) after each uplink; ADR mechanism. | REGISTRATION |
| `CIT-FCC-15247` | 47 CFR § 15.247 | eCFR / US GPO | https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/section-15.247 | Frequency-hopping and digital-modulation rules for 902–928 MHz, including per-channel dwell limits. eCFR blocks automated fetching; open in a browser. | ACCESS-LIMITED |

